---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { journey } from '../data/journey';
import { skills, practice, education } from '../data/about';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait/shavi-formal.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Shavi Saini is a Computer Science Engineering student working in cybersecurity: network threat analytics, web and API security testing, and hands-on lab practice."
  page="about"
>
  <div class="page page--narrow">
    <div class="about-lead">
      <PageHeader
        eyebrow="About"
        title="Shavi Saini"
        lede="A Computer Science Engineering student working in cybersecurity — network threat analytics, web and API security testing, and the lab practice behind both."
      />
      <figure class="about-lead__portrait">
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt="Portrait of Shavi Saini in a white shirt and maroon tie"
          widths={[240, 360, 480]}
          sizes="(min-width: 46rem) 11rem, 38vw"
          quality={78}
        />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="intro prose" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Most of what I know I learned by building something and then finding out where it was
        wrong. <a href={href('/netra/')}>NETRA</a> is the clearest example: a passive network
        threat analytics prototype where the hardest problems were not detection at all, but
        deciding what a detector is allowed to say, and making a missing measurement stay
        missing instead of quietly becoming a zero.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside that I work through web and API security the same way — intercepting and
        modifying requests, exploiting the vulnerability classes in a lab I control, and
        writing down what the finding actually proves. I finished the Google Cybersecurity
        Professional Certificate in 2025, a 45-day security internship with an A+ grade in
        2026, and I compete in CTFs when I can.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am looking for security engineering and security analyst internships where the work
        involves real telemetry and real evidence. If that is you — or if you are a student
        working through the same problems —
        <a href={site.links.linkedin} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          LinkedIn is the easiest place to start
        </a>.
        The <a href={href('/resume/')}>resume</a> is the compressed version of the same record.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Section id="journey" index="01" title="Journey">
      <ol class="timeline">
        {
          journey.map((milestone, index) => (
            <li class="milestone" data-reveal style={`--reveal-delay: ${index * 60}ms`}>
              <span class="milestone__date mono">{milestone.date}</span>
              <span class="milestone__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div class="milestone__body">
                <h3 class="milestone__title">{milestone.title}</h3>
                <p class="milestone__detail">{milestone.detail}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </Section>

    <Section id="skills" index="02" title="Skills">
      <dl class="skills" data-reveal>
        {
          skills.map((group) => (
            <div class="skills__group">
              <dt>{group.group}</dt>
              <dd>
                <ul>
                  {group.items.map((item) => (
                    <li>{item}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p class="note">
        No percentage bars. A skill is either something I have used on a documented piece of
        work or something I am still learning, and a number would not tell you which.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="practice" index="03" title="Lab practice">
      <p class="note note--lead">
        These are structured exercises in a lab I built, not original projects. The
        distinction matters: anyone who has run them will know the difference, and calling
        them projects would cost more credibility than it buys.
      </p>
      <ul class="practice" data-reveal>
        {
          practice.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.detail}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section id="education" index="04" title="Education">
      <dl class="education" data-reveal>
        {
          education.map((entry) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{entry.qualification}</dt>
              <dd>
                {entry.institution && <span>{entry.institution}</span>}
                <span class="mono">{entry.detail}</span>
              </dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </Section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-lead {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-items: end;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .about-lead :global(.page-header) {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-lead__portrait {
    margin: 0;
    width: min(10.5rem, 42vw);
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-figure);
    background: var(--bg-sunken);
  }

  .about-lead__portrait :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 12%;
  }

  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .about-lead {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 11rem;
      align-items: start;
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }

    .about-lead__portrait {
      width: 100%;
      margin-top: var(--space-8);
    }
  }

  .intro {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- timeline */

  .timeline {
    display: grid;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .milestone {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding-block: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .milestone:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .milestone__date {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .milestone__mark {
    display: none;
  }

  .milestone__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .milestone__title {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .milestone__detail {
    max-width: 66ch;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.89rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .timeline::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      left: 7.05rem;
      top: 0.55rem;
      bottom: 0.55rem;
      width: 1px;
      background: linear-gradient(
        to bottom,
        var(--accent-line),
        var(--line) 18%,
        var(--line) 82%,
        transparent
      );
    }

    .milestone {
      grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 0.75rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-4);
      border-top: 0;
      padding-block: var(--space-5);
    }

    .milestone:first-child {
      padding-top: 0;
    }

    .milestone__mark {
      display: block;
      width: 9px;
      height: 9px;
      margin-top: 0.45rem;
      border-radius: 50%;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent);
      background: var(--bg);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--bg);
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
    }
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------- skills */

  .skills {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .skills__group {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .skills dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.11em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .skills dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .skills ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .skills li {
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    transition:
      border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease),
      color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease),
      background-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease);
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .skills li:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent-line);
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--accent-wash);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .skills__group {
      grid-template-columns: 11rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-5);
      align-items: baseline;
    }
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------- practice */

  .practice {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .practice li {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
  }

  .practice h3 {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
  }

  .practice p {
    max-width: 68ch;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.89rem;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ education */

  .education {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .education dt {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .education dd {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .note {
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .note--lead {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
